===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[grab]] or [[seize]] by the collar or [[neck]].
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[place]] a collar on, to [[fit]] with one.
#: {{ux|en|'''Collar''' and leash aggressive dogs.}}
#* {{quote-song|en|title=[[w:Orange Crush (song)|Orange Crush]]|author=[[w:R.E.M.|R.E.M.]]|album=[[w:Green (R.E.M. album)|Green]]|date=1988-11-08|text=(Follow me, don't follow me.) I've got my spine, I've got my orange crush.</br>('''Collar''' me, don't '''collar''' me.) I've got my spine, I've got my orange crush.}}
# To [[surround]] or [[encircle]].
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[seize]], [[capture]] or [[detain]].
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[steal]].
#* {{quote-book|1=en|year=1918|author=w:Norman Lindsay|title=The Magic Pudding|publisher=Angus and Robertson|location=Sydney|page=52|passage="Ho, aboard the ''Salt Junk Sarah'',<br>Rollin" home across the line,<br>The Bo'sun '''collared''' the Captain's hat<br>And threw it in the brine.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[preempt]], control stringently and exclusively.
# {{senseid|en|arrest}} {{lb|en|law enforcement|transitive}} To [[arrest]].
#* {{quote-web|1=en|date=2025-05-15|title=Europe’s free-speech problem|author=|work=The Economist|url=https://archive.is/seOtp|text=Britain’s police are especially zealous. Officers spend thousands of hours sifting through potentially offensive posts and arrest 30 people a day. Among those '''collared''' were a man who ranted about immigration on Facebook and a couple who criticised their daughter’s primary school.}}
# {{lb|en|figuratively|transitive}} To [[bind]] in [[conversation]].
#: {{ux|en|I managed to '''collar''' Fred in the office for an hour.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=19 Dec 81|volume=9|number=22|journal=Gay Community News|page=8|author=Nancy Wechsler;Christine Delphy|title=Politics In France|text=They go in and lobby, '''collar''' the representatives and ask: are you for or against?}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To roll up (beef or other meat) and [[bind]] it with [[string]] [[preparatory]] to [[cook]]ing.
# {{lb|en|transitive|BDSM}} To bind (a [[submissive]]) to a [[dominant]] under specific conditions or obligations.

